    <detaileddescription>
<para>Given a collection of vectors, w_i, find a collection of vectors x_i such that x_i is orthogonal to w_j for i != j, and &lt;x_i, w_i&gt; = &lt;w_i, w_i&gt;</para><para>This is done by performing GramSchmidt on the other vectors and then projecting onto the orthogonal space.</para><para>This class is tested in <verbatim>MatricesTest::testOrthogonalProjection();</verbatim> </para>    </detaileddescription>
